": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "By 2024?", "t0": 92.94, "t1": 94.3, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Attaie Healthcare · Medicare payments", "rows": [["2021", "$261,954"], ["2022", "$452,035"], ["2023", "$2,113,352"], ["2024", "$4,955,974"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.4]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Almost 5 million dollars.", "t0": 94.3, "t1": 95.73, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$4,955,974", "label": "paid in 2024", "sub": "19 times as much in 3 years"}, "emph": ["Almost"], "wt": [0.04, 0.38, 0.6, 0.88]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "story[4]"], "text": "Attaie goes the other way: 57.8 percent left alive, above the middle.", "t0": 96.25, "t1": 100.7, "shot": "b25s", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Attaie, discharged alive, 2025", "57.8%"], "b": ["California middle", "48.1%"], "kicker": "The State’s own report"}, "emph": ["57.8 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.52, 0.62, 0.83, 1.59, 2.25, 2.6, 2.85, 3.25, 3.47, 3.86, 4.11, 4.2]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[14]", "status"], "text": "Medicare’s revoked list has 479 hospices, 402 in California. None of these eight is on it.", "t0": 100.92, "t1": 107.07, "shot": "b26r", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Hospices on Medicare’s revoked list", "479"], "b": ["In California", "402"], "kicker": "Medicare’s revoked list, July 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.49, 0.84, 1.12, 1.3, 1.52, 1.77, 2.31, 3.29, 3.52, 3.73, 3.95, 4.05, 5.07, 5.26, 5.33, 5.52, 5.74, 5.89, 6.05]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[15]", "innocent[8]"], "text": "The State’s own counts show no enforcement action at the five hospices looked up.", "t0": 107.19, "t1": 111.09, "shot": "b26s", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no State enforcement action at any of the five hospices looked up", "kicker": "Cal Health Find, 21 November 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.44, 0.65, 1.04, 1.3, 1.47, 1.98, 2.44, 2.59, 2.69, 2.95, 3.43, 3.69]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "status"], "text": "But fast growth alone proves nothing. The records don’t show any patient was ineligible, or any claim false.", "t0": 111.21, "t1": 116.83, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any patient was ineligible", "That any claim was false"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.33, 0.53, 0.78, 1.02, 2.07, 2.27, 2.68, 2.89, 3.11, 3.29, 3.67, 3.83, 4.52, 4.72, 4.91, 5.19]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? Ownership files, and why two hospices filed no State report.", "t0": 116.95, "t1": 121.44, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Change-of-ownership filings: who owned each when certified?"}, {"who": "", "what": "Why two hospices filed no State report while Medicare paid them"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.29, 0.59, 1.35, 1.84, 2.31, 2.44, 2.63, 2.86, 3.39, 3.69, 3.84, 4.08]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "It’s a statistical screen, weaker for Grace And Glory. No authority has acted against any of them.", "t0": 121.56, "t1": 127.19, "shot": "b30", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.25, 0.91, 1.86, 2.3, 2.45, 2.7, 2.8, 3.76, 3.95, 4.35, 4.48, 4.75, 5.02, 5.23, 5.33]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.31, "t1": 129.25, "shot": "b31", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.44, 0.51, 1.05, 1.25, 1.34]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "Why look here", "lead1": "Lead 1 · A Plus Prime Care", "lead2": "Lead 2 · Grace and Glory", "lead3": "Lead 3 · Best Hospice Provider", "lead4": "Lead 4 · Home Connect", "lead5": "Lead 5 · Attaie Healthcare", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "map", "hook": "person"}